\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Oriented graded posets, molecules, joins, Gray products, and geometric pasting are optional presentations and tools after the algebraic root is validated. Every proposed equivalence between a geometric category and an arity category specifies morphisms as well as objects. A geometric presentation does not determine the root by itself. A renderer can begin with the validated elementary syntax.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{A large general substrate should follow evidence that it helps the chosen model.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Making the general pasting theorem and all geometric shape comparisons prerequisites for the first nondiscrete root example.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-kr-0012}/13/14 are deferred geometric comparisons, with exact statements required before promotion from proposed to stated.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{later (after \ref{ms-0003}, specific clients determine priority).}
}
